# Period selection without parallel response trees

## Problem

Details currently fetch complete histories, then `services/entity_details.rs` computes mandatory three-period GBP totals plus historical-only ancillary summaries. Rankings filters twice to current term (`outbound/rankings.rs` SQL and `services/rankings.rs`) and truncates after grouping. The change must scope all ancillary summaries and declarations together without making headline totals partial or changing identity. Retain the existing response nesting, exact amount strings, category scope differences, and fixed top-ten behavior.

## Usage (caller's view)

```rust
// HTTP boundary: missing means current term; invalid explicit value returns 400.
let period: DeclarationPeriod = query.period.unwrap_or_default();
let request = path.id.parse::<MemberDetailsRequest>()?.with_period(period);
let details = service.member(request).await?;
// details.summary.declared_totals still contains all three complete totals;
// details.summary.currencies and details.declarations contain this period only.

let boards = rankings.rankings(period).await?;
// Each board is filtered before grouping, exact sorting and truncation.
```

```ts
// SvelteKit load, shared by summary/history; URL owns selection.
const period = readPeriod(url.searchParams);
const result = await loadDetails(route, period, request.signal, fetch, origin);
return { model: { kind: "detail", route, period, result } };

// All identity and category/view links preserve selection and search context.
const href = memberHref(id, "history", url.searchParams);
const metric = selectedDeclaredTotal(details.summary.declaredTotals, period);
```

```svelte
<!-- Feature composes the shared native-link primitive. -->
<PeriodSelector {period} url={page.url} />
<DeclaredTotals totals={details.summary.declaredTotals} {period} />
<!-- On history only, dates refine the already scoped declarations. -->
{#key period}<MemberHistory {details} />{/key}
```

## Shape

One domain vocabulary and one date-rule owner, in `domain/models/declaration_period.rs`:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Deserialize, Serialize)]
#[serde(rename_all = "kebab-case")]
pub enum DeclarationPeriod {
    Historical,
    #[default] CurrentTerm,
    CurrentYear,
}
impl FromStr for DeclarationPeriod { /* exhaustive canonical wire spelling; invalid => error */ }
impl DeclarationPeriod {
    pub fn resolve(self, year: CalendarYear) -> RegistrationPeriod { todo!() }
}
// Private fields prevent callers constructing inconsistent bounds/undated policy.
pub struct RegistrationPeriod { /* kind, optional inclusive start/exclusive end */ }
impl RegistrationPeriod {
    pub fn includes(&self, registered_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>) -> bool { todo!() }
    // Historical includes undated; both dated scopes exclude it.
    // Current year is [Jan 1 UTC, next Jan 1 UTC), NOT year-to-date.
    pub fn bounds(&self) -> (Option<DateTime<Utc>>, Option<DateTime<Utc>>) { todo!() }
}
```

Move/reuse `CalendarYear` and `CurrentParliamentStart` behind this owner. Their existing implementations must delegate to the resolved period rule or be removed after callers migrate; do not retain independent `includes` rules. Capture `Utc::now()` once per service operation, derive one year, and use it for selected scope and all headline totals. Enum parsing uses its derived representation or exhaustive match, never a second string allowlist.

Extend existing private-field `MemberDetailsRequest` and `FunderDetailsRequest` with `period: DeclarationPeriod`, `with_period`, and `period()`; keep ID `FromStr` as the current-term default constructor. Existing `EntityDetailsService` method signatures and response structures survive. Rankings becomes `rankings(period: DeclarationPeriod)`. HTTP adds typed `Query<PeriodQuery>` extraction to all three handlers; framework rejection maps malformed explicit values to 400.

Entity services retain existing full-history repository reads. In both summarizers:

1. Observe each original declaration into `DeclaredTotalsAggregate`, without filtering.
2. Retain only declarations included by the selected resolved scope.
3. Compute ancillary currency/category/recipient/party/count/date summaries from retained declarations only. For funders this happens before recipient sorting/truncation.
4. Return original identity/profile unchanged, scoped declaration stream, scoped summary fields, complete three-period totals in their current nesting.

`DeclaredTotalsAggregate::observe` uses the canonical period resolver for its term/year membership checks. Its historical/current-term/current-year aggregates remain explicit fields, preserving the mandatory output type. Add one selected `PeriodAggregate` for member ancillary summaries rather than consuming `aggregate.historical.finish()` as today. This avoids a mutable enum-indexed map, optional headline fields, and multiple copies of the detail graph.

Ranking repository signature:

```rust
fn ranking_declarations(&self, period: RegistrationPeriod)
    -> impl Future<Output=Result<Vec<RankingDeclaration>, RankingsError>> + Send;
```

Use the resolved bound pair in one `sqlx::query!` predicate: `($1::timestamptz IS NULL OR registration_date >= $1) AND ($2::timestamptz IS NULL OR registration_date < $2)`. Historical unbounded nulls include undated rows. Dated intervals exclude undated through SQL comparisons. The service's defensive membership check uses the same scope object, so duplication is mechanical rather than independent policy. Keep `Rankings.current_term_start` metadata for compatibility; it remains the fixed term boundary even on other selections. Do not relabel it as the active scope. Member boards retain all categories; the other boards retain DonationSupport only.

Frontend `lib/declaration-period.ts` owns an `as const` option list (id, requested label, totals key), derives `DeclarationPeriod`, parses URL selection, selects the authoritative total, and builds selection URLs. The frontend has no date-boundary logic; it only forwards canonical selected ID to backend. Missing defaults current-term; invalid UI URL canonicalizes to current-term (backend direct invalid query remains 400). `+page.server.ts` models carry typed selection, both server clients append it to API requests. Existing amount/count/currency parsers remain unchanged and all three total fields stay mandatory.

Navigation helper retains existing `q` semantics plus selected period, for `memberHref`, `funderHref`, ranking rows/category links, and search links. Period-change builder deletes any date/page refinement keys while preserving category, view path, and q. Existing custom dates are local history-only refinements: key history components by period to clear dates and pagination on selection changes. This requires no server custom-date API and no client reimplementation of named-period filtering.

`DeclaredTotals.svelte` becomes a single selected metric over the still-complete totals model. Avoid using selected `firstRegisteredAt` to label the historical total; historical label is simply existing “Historical declared amounts”. Backend selected date range remains scoped like the other data.

Shared UI extends `ViewLinks`/`ViewLink` with a documented typed compact/segmented variant if current capability cannot display this control. `PeriodSelector.svelte` stays a feature adapter producing URLs and option labels. Shared UI accepts links/current state only; neutral action/focus tokens, native anchors, `aria-current`, wrapping on mobile. Export reusable variant types, document and demonstrate gallery usage, add accessibility and navigation tests.

The public surface hides date semantics and all aggregation; callers pass one typed selection. Repository read optimization receives a resolved scope rather than owning calendar rules. No response envelope, separate endpoint family, database migration, or total fallback is needed.

## Synthesis decision

Candidate supplied for orchestrator synthesis; not selected yet.

## Tradeoffs accepted

- Accept complete detail-history reads in exchange for unchanged repository contracts and provably complete headline totals. Detail history was already read fully.
- Accept independent wire vocabulary declarations across Rust/TypeScript in exchange for no codegen infrastructure; boundary integration tests exercise all three values. Frontend defines its type from its option data rather than duplicating its own allowlist.
- Accept fixed term metadata in rankings responses in exchange for response compatibility; active selection belongs to the request/page model.

## Alternatives considered

- Return a `periods: {historical, currentTerm, currentYear}` tree containing three full detail summaries/histories: callers must choose matching subtrees and identities; response size and invariant surface increase while hiding little more than service-side selection. Rejected.
- Push selected filtering into detail SQL and separately query headlines: exposes two coordinated reads and snapshot consistency requirements, adds persistence work despite already having complete histories, and risks incomplete mandatory totals. Rejected for this change; a future measured performance need could justify a snapshot-owned read operation.

## Implementation reconciliation

No implementation performed. Avoid adding `period` to response models unless an actual consumer needs an echo; SSR already owns selection.

## Open questions and risks

- Does `sqlx`'s actual registration column type require `timestamp` or `timestamptz` casts? Preserve the existing time adapter and verify query metadata against the development schema.
- Can existing ViewLinks satisfy the compact control without a new variant? Inspect actual rendered styles before expanding shared UI.

## Next implementation step

Add canonical period types and deterministic boundary tests, then migrate existing headline membership checks before changing endpoint scoping.

## Acceptance evidence

Backend tests: exact inclusive term boundary; full year including future-dated December and exclusion at following January; undated historical-only; empty/zero/null/foreign/unknown currency; unknown categories; no-entry declarations; identical occurrence multiplicity; all three headline totals invariant across selected scope; ancillary counts/date/currency/category/recipient/party scopes; top ten after scoping with historical-only leaders and >10 candidates; per-board category differences; invalid API period 400.
Frontend tests: SSR selected metric and all scoped sections on rankings/member/funder summary/history; default/current year/historical links; preserve period across category/view/entity navigation; dates/history page reset; complete totals parser rejection when one missing; native keyboard links and narrow layout; neutral focus/action styling; desktop screenshots from branch application.
